  "notes": "Found on 2026-11-25 by a search over the cyclic group of order 267, written as Z_3 x Z_89. With s = 88, for which s^2 = 1 modulo 267 (s is 1 modulo 3 and -1 modulo 89), row A as submitted is unchanged by k -> -sk, row D is unchanged by k -> sk, and row C is row B carried by k -> sk: C(k) = B(sk). All four rows are unchanged by multiplication by 91, of order 11 modulo 267. The row sums are 1, 23, 23, 3. The search is an exact join over rows constant on the orbits of these maps, exhaustive for this s and this group of multipliers and for nothing else; the run record gives its patterns and counts. The Goethals-Seidel array of these rows is a Hadamard matrix of order 1068. The rows also give a symmetric Hadamard matrix of order 1068, by a variant of the propus array that was worked out for this board and has not been reviewed; the run record states it, and the verifier does not check that matrix. The run record lists what was read on 2026-11-25 about the status of the order: a census dated May 2025 lists v = 267 as undecided for symmetric Hadamard matrices of order 4v, and the search of the literature and public repositories found no symmetric Hadamard matrix of order 1068. This reports the search and does not claim priority, and the result has not been reviewed."
